{
  "title": "Immunization → drug_exposure (CVX)",
  "notes": "The drug branch is fanned in from several FHIR source resources that all land in OMOP `drug_exposure`, each with its own stage-2 SQL and a distinct `drug_type_concept_id` constant:\n\n- `MedicationRequest__drug_exposure.sql` — prescription order. `drug_type_concept_id = 38000177` ('Prescription written'). RxNorm preferred, NDC fallback (inner JOIN on 'Maps to' → standard Drug, so an unmapped code yields NO row). `drug_exposure_start_date = end_date = authoredOn`; the `_datetime` pair is `authoredOn::timestamp`. `person_id ← subject`, `visit_occurrence_id ← encounter`, `provider_id ← requester`. Status filter drops `entered-in-error / cancelled / draft / unknown`.\n- `MedicationAdministration__drug_exposure.sql` — drug actually given. `drug_type_concept_id = 38000179` (vocab name in this bundle: 'Physician administered drug (identified as procedure)'). RxNorm > NDC > SNOMED (inner JOIN to standard Drug). `start = end = effectiveDateTime`. `person_id ← subject`, `visit_occurrence_id ← context` (R4 'context'). NO provider mapped → `provider_id` NULL. Status filter (NULL treated as 'completed') drops `entered-in-error / not-done / unknown`.\n- `Immunization__drug_exposure.sql` — point-in-time vaccination. `drug_type_concept_id = 32827` ('EHR encounter record'). CVX preferred, RxNorm fallback. Uses a **LEFT JOIN** to 'Maps to', so a CVX code with no crosswalk still produces a row with `drug_concept_id = 0` while `drug_source_concept_id` keeps the CVX source concept. `start = end = occurrenceDateTime`. `person_id ← patient`, `visit_occurrence_id ← encounter`. NO provider. Status filter drops `entered-in-error / not-done`.\n\nGrounding notes from the live May-2026 Athena bundle:\n- RxNorm 896209 → standard Drug 40169281 (self-map). RxNorm 1665060 (cefazolin 2000 MG Injection) → 46287345 (self-map). RxNorm 797752 (hepatitis B surface antigen vaccine) → 528323 (self-map). All three are vocabulary_id='RxNorm', domain_id='Drug', standard 'S', and 'Maps to' themselves.\n- The CVX vocabulary is the real OHDSI CVX (Athena bundle 2026-07-07, ~288 concepts with normal concept_ids ~4021xxxx; many are Standard 'S' Drug concepts that 'Maps to' themselves). CVX 08 = 40213304 ('hepatitis B vaccine, pediatric…', Standard, self-map), so variant (f) (CVX+RxNorm, CVX wins prio) resolves to 40213304 from the CVX coding. The only unmapped CVX is code 99 'RESERVED - do not use' (40213262, non-standard, no 'Maps to') → variant (d) uses it to exercise the LEFT-JOIN zero-fallback (drug_concept_id 0, drug_source_concept_id = the CVX source concept 40213262). Variant (c) still exercises the RxNorm fallback path via an Immunization carrying only an RxNorm coding.\n- Datetime casts: stage-2 uses `::timestamp` on the FHIR dateTime string with a `+00:00` offset, which Postgres truncates to wall-clock (e.g. '2023-12-07T18:39:19+00:00'::timestamp = '2023-12-07 18:39:19') — NO UTC shift (unlike Procedure). Confirmed against the actual cdm_ours_fhir.drug_exposure row for Synthea MedicationAdministration 18071d58-3d43-cb2e-15ff-b72638e1b241.\n\nEvery non-NULL drug_exposure column is asserted; the columns the stage-2 SELECTs hard-code to NULL (verbatim_end_date, stop_reason, refills, quantity, days_supply, sig, route_concept_id, lot_number, visit_detail_id, route_source_value, dose_unit_source_value) are omitted and therefore asserted NULL. drug_exposure is the ONLY target table for this branch; an `omop:{}` case asserts zero rows everywhere.",
